    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278-a2">

                <pb facs="0667" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg571"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 179.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to Mr.
                            Ethéart.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 8,
                        1879</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Your dispatch of the 7th instant
                    has been received, and in reply thereto I have the honor to state that no
                    refugee connected with the insurrection of which you speak has been accorded
                    protection under my flag.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
